{"toolCallId":"call_1f147e9938c3493da578a0a054190e24","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the baseline: run the existing vitest file and save the text and JSON stdout for one fixture packet (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T002 Confirm which variable holds the figure each reporter prints, and note that `output_text` keeps it in a function local (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Declare `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside the other option globals in section 3 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent` arm to the argument loop, testing `$#` before reading `$2` so `set -u` cannot abort on a missing value (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Reject a non-integer and anything outside 0-100 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr and exit 1 before any file is read (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Document the option and both exit statuses in `show_help` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Replace the final `exit 0` with an explicit `if` that exits 3 below the threshold and 0 at or above it, reading the same figure the reporter printed (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Add vitest cases for below, equal, above, invalid value, missing value, output equality and a missing `--file` target (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Run the vitest file from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime` and confirm every case passes\n- [ ] T010 Run the script with and without the flag on the same packet and confirm an empty `diff` for both the text and `--json` reports\n- [ ] T011 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet and reconcile any deviation back into `spec.md` and `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Threshold behavior demonstrated on a real packet: exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at or above it\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Script under change**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the baseline: run the existing vitest file and save the text and JSON stdout for one fixture packet (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T002 Confirm which variable holds the figure each reporter prints, and note that `output_text` keeps it in a function local (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Declare `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside the other option globals in section 3 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent` arm to the argument loop, testing `$#` before reading `$2` so `set -u` cannot abort on a missing value (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Reject a non-integer and anything outside 0-100 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr and exit 1 before any file is read (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Document the option and both exit statuses in `show_help` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Replace the final `exit 0` with an explicit `if` that exits 3 below the threshold and 0 at or above it, reading the same figure the reporter printed (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Add vitest cases for below, equal, above, invalid value, missing value, output equality and a missing `--file` target (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T012 Implements REQ-007: add `min_percent_met` to the JSON reporter, emitted only when `--min-percent` was passed, true when `Overall Completion` is at or above N and false otherwise (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Run the vitest file from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime` and confirm every case passes\n- [ ] T010 Run the script with and without the flag on the same packet and confirm an empty `diff` for both the text and `--json` reports\n- [ ] T011 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet and reconcile any deviation back into `spec.md` and `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Threshold behavior demonstrated on a real packet: exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at or above it\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Script under change**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_23a0e320419445dbb4ff6a992ca4b55a","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports a completion percentage and then always exits 0, so a caller that wants to gate on the number has to parse stdout. A --min-percent option turns that check into an exit status without changing the report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\n  - \"min-percent exit code gate\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then exits 0 unconditionally, whatever the number says. A caller that wants to stop on a packet below N% has to capture stdout, pull the percentage out of a decorated text block (or read `overall_completion` from `--json`), and repeat the comparison itself. That parsing is brittle: the report is wrapped in box-drawing rules and a status line, so a formatting change breaks every caller silently. The script already computes the number; only the verdict is missing.\n\n### Purpose\n\nLet a caller gate on completion with one flag and one exit status, while every figure the script reports stays exactly as it is.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- A `--min-percent <N>` option on `calculate-completeness.sh`, with N an integer from 0 to 100.\n- Exit status 3 when the reported completion is below N, and 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Argument validation for the option: a missing value, a non-integer and a value outside 0-100 are user errors.\n- Help text and tests for the new option.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- The percentage math, the placeholder patterns, the text layout and the JSON schema - the feature adds a verdict, not a new report.\n- A short alias (`-m`) or an `--min-percent=N` spelling - the request names one form, and more spellings are a separate decision.\n- Wiring the flag into hooks, CI or `check-completion.sh` - callers adopt it after this lands.\n- The unguarded `$2` read on `--file` - it has the same latent fault today, and repairing it would change behavior outside this request.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Parse the option, validate N, document it in help, derive the exit status from the reported percentage |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cover the threshold boundaries, invalid input, and unchanged output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` anywhere in the argument list, with N an integer from 0 to 100 | `--min-percent 80 <packet>` runs the report; `--min-percent` with no value and `--min-percent abc` each exit 1 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N, and 0 when it is at or above N | A packet reporting 40% exits 3 with `--min-percent 41` and 0 with `--min-percent 40` |\n| REQ-003 | The report itself is unchanged | `diff` of stdout with and without the flag is empty, in text and `--json` modes, for both a folder and a `--file` target |\n| REQ-004 | Compare the same figure the report prints | Folder mode compares `Overall Completion`; `--file` mode compares that file's `Completion`, the only figure that mode reports |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-005 | `--help` documents the option and both exit statuses | Help output contains `--min-percent <N>` and names exit 3 as \"below threshold\" |\n| REQ-006 | Tests cover the boundary and the invalid inputs | The vitest file passes with cases for below, equal, above, invalid and missing value |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: A caller gates on completion with one flag and no stdout parsing - `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 <packet>` returns 0 or 3, and nothing else about the run changes.\n- **SC-002**: The text and JSON reports for a given packet are byte-identical with and without the option.\n- **SC-003**: The two tests already in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` still pass unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | The script exits 1 today when `bc` is absent | The option adds no new dependency |\n| Risk | Exit status 3 already means \"system error\" in the spec-script taxonomy | Medium - a caller that reads 3 as an I/O failure could misread a low score | State the meaning in `--help`, and treat 3 as \"below threshold\" only when the flag was passed |\n| Risk | The reported percentage is rounded to a whole number before comparison | Low - 89.6% prints as 90 and passes `--min-percent 90` | Document that the gate compares the printed integer, not the raw fraction |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns a bare `(( percentage < N ))` into a silent abort | Medium - the script already carries a comment about this pattern at its clamp | Write the decision as an explicit `if`, matching the existing clamp style |\n| Risk | The printed figure carries defaults: an empty packet reports 100%, a missing `--file` target reports 0% | Low - a gate on an empty folder passes | Document both defaults in the plan and cover the missing-file case in the tests |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone blocking. Resolved while writing this spec:\n\n- Does the option apply in `--file` mode? Yes, against that file's `Completion`, because `Overall Completion` does not exist in that mode (REQ-004).\n- Does \"output unchanged\" cover `--help`? No. The calculation report is unchanged; help gains one option line, which REQ-005 requires.\n- What status for a bad N? 1, the script's existing status for a bad argument.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports a completion percentage and then always exits 0, so a caller that wants to gate on the number has to parse stdout. A --min-percent option turns that check into an exit status without changing the report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\n  - \"min-percent exit code gate\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then exits 0 unconditionally, whatever the number says. A caller that wants to stop on a packet below N% has to capture stdout, pull the percentage out of a decorated text block (or read `overall_completion` from `--json`), and repeat the comparison itself. That parsing is brittle: the report is wrapped in box-drawing rules and a status line, so a formatting change breaks every caller silently. The script already computes the number; only the verdict is missing.\n\n### Purpose\n\nLet a caller gate on completion with one flag and one exit status, while every figure the script reports stays exactly as it is.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- A `--min-percent <N>` option on `calculate-completeness.sh`, with N an integer from 0 to 100.\n- Exit status 3 when the reported completion is below N, and 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Argument validation for the option: a missing value, a non-integer and a value outside 0-100 are user errors.\n- Help text and tests for the new option.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- The percentage math, the placeholder patterns, the text layout and the JSON schema - the feature adds a verdict, not a new report.\n- A short alias (`-m`) or an `--min-percent=N` spelling - the request names one form, and more spellings are a separate decision.\n- Wiring the flag into hooks, CI or `check-completion.sh` - callers adopt it after this lands.\n- The unguarded `$2` read on `--file` - it has the same latent fault today, and repairing it would change behavior outside this request.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Parse the option, validate N, document it in help, derive the exit status from the reported percentage |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cover the threshold boundaries, invalid input, and unchanged output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` anywhere in the argument list, with N an integer from 0 to 100 | `--min-percent 80 <packet>` runs the report; `--min-percent` with no value and `--min-percent abc` each exit 1 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N, and 0 when it is at or above N | A packet reporting 40% exits 3 with `--min-percent 41` and 0 with `--min-percent 40` |\n| REQ-003 | The report itself is unchanged | `diff` of stdout with and without the flag is empty, in text and `--json` modes, for both a folder and a `--file` target |\n| REQ-004 | Compare the same figure the report prints | Folder mode compares `Overall Completion`; `--file` mode compares that file's `Completion`, the only figure that mode reports |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-005 | `--help` documents the option and both exit statuses | Help output contains `--min-percent <N>` and names exit 3 as \"below threshold\" |\n| REQ-006 | Tests cover the boundary and the invalid inputs | The vitest file passes with cases for below, equal, above, invalid and missing value |\n| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean field `min_percent_met`, true when `Overall Completion` is at or above N and false when it is below | `--json --min-percent 80 <packet>` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` for a packet reporting 80% and `false` for one reporting 79%; the field is absent from `--json` output when `--min-percent` is not passed |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: A caller gates on completion with one flag and no stdout parsing - `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 <packet>` returns 0 or 3, and nothing else about the run changes.\n- **SC-002**: The text and JSON reports for a given packet are byte-identical with and without the option.\n- **SC-003**: The two tests already in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` still pass unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | The script exits 1 today when `bc` is absent | The option adds no new dependency |\n| Risk | Exit status 3 already means \"system error\" in the spec-script taxonomy | Medium - a caller that reads 3 as an I/O failure could misread a low score | State the meaning in `--help`, and treat 3 as \"below threshold\" only when the flag was passed |\n| Risk | The reported percentage is rounded to a whole number before comparison | Low - 89.6% prints as 90 and passes `--min-percent 90` | Document that the gate compares the printed integer, not the raw fraction |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns a bare `(( percentage < N ))` into a silent abort | Medium - the script already carries a comment about this pattern at its clamp | Write the decision as an explicit `if`, matching the existing clamp style |\n| Risk | The printed figure carries defaults: an empty packet reports 100%, a missing `--file` target reports 0% | Low - a gate on an empty folder passes | Document both defaults in the plan and cover the missing-file case in the tests |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone blocking. Resolved while writing this spec:\n\n- Does the option apply in `--file` mode? Yes, against that file's `Completion`, because `Overall Completion` does not exist in that mode (REQ-004).\n- Does \"output unchanged\" cover `--help`? No. The calculation report is unchanged; help gains one option line, which REQ-005 requires.\n- What status for a bad N? 1, the script's existing status for a bad argument.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
